  "body": "Adds the finish3d `gap_link` parameter: a dropdown with `Jump` (default, today's retract/clearance hop, unchanged) and `Straight` (one straight Feed link between the run ends at their own tip height - no rise, no traverse, no plunge).\n\nWhat changed:\n- `camcraft_motion::finishing3d`: new `GapLink` enum (default `Jump`) and `Finish3DParams.gap_link`; new `gaplink.rs` with the `Straight` verdict; the `emit_runs` chain tries the straight link on a break the `ramp` diagonal refused, and keeps the plain hop when the verdict says no.\n- The law: the line is fixed (both run ends are legal tangent centers by the march's own construction), so the exact segment-triangle sweep of the move at the budget `r - TOUCH_EPS` answers the whole question. Grazing rims pass, a real bite refuses, and a refusal takes the `Jump` hop byte for byte as every older file ran.\n- Serpentine fix: a raster line broken by openings now runs back WHOLE (`pieces.reverse()` plus each piece's points). Reversing only the points made every gap link jump back across the whole field instead of crossing its gap. This shortens the existing `Jump` traverses on broken lines too.\n- Project file: the words `jump` and `straight`, written always like `ramp` - no version step-up; older files read as `jump`. The digest takes tag `0x4D` plus a variant byte only when the choice is not `Jump`, so ops that hop as before keep their old stamp.\n- UI: \"Gap link\" combo (Jump / Straight) in the Mill 3D passes section. MCP: the same words ride the existing `edit_operation` params door and undo.\n\nHow tested: `crates/motion/tests/finish3d_gaplink.rs` - 6 pins: the jump pin (byte-for-byte old behavior), straight links over a holed plate at the run height, every straight link kept clear of the facets (exact sweep scan, Prime Directive), straight refused over a biting slot keeps the plain hop (byte-for-byte `Jump` crossings), and every hop traverse spans one gap, never the field (fails on the pre-fix serpentine with a 31.7 mm field jump). Round-trip pins in `crates/app/tests/project_roundtrip.rs` (jump/straight/absent) and the params-door test in `crates/app/tests/mcp.rs`. Quick gate on the touched crates green; the finish3d release verdict lanes and `golden_cl` / `operations` / `project_roundtrip` / mcp / ui structural suites green.\n\nNot exercised: geodesic ring chains (keep the plain hop, unchanged); patterns other than the march rasters.\n\nGUI check: the maintainer approved the two-option surface (`Jump` as before, `Straight` as here) in chat after testing the Straight link over the holes in his 171 mm STEP part on an intermediate build; the `Straight` law itself is unchanged in this rebuild. A release build of this head is available for a re-test.\n\nChangelog: finish3d gap_link: a straight link across gap openings (Jump / Straight) (#1708, PR #1713)\n\nBase note: the head branch is on the tbrasselle/Camcraft fork (the gh account has no write access on this repo); it branches from this repo's main at 101d82f9, so it merges clean.\n\nFixes #1708\n",
